  "Question": "The expression \\(\\sqrt{\\dfrac43}-\\sqrt{\\dfrac34}\\) is equal to:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{6}\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{6}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{-3}}6\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5\\sqrt3}{6}\\)",
    "E": "\\(1\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Rewrite both terms as multiples of \\(\\sqrt3\\), so we can subtract their coefficients. Using the positive square roots,\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac43}\n=\\frac2{\\sqrt3}\n=\\frac{2\\sqrt3}{3},\n\\qquad\n\\sqrt{\\frac34}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt{\\frac43}-\\sqrt{\\frac34}\n&=\\left(\\frac23-\\frac12\\right)\\sqrt3\\\\\n&=\\frac16\\sqrt3.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe value is \\(\\sqrt3/6\\), choice A.",
